1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,788
Two names. One ambiguous type.

2
00:00:01,868 --> 00:00:03,140
This factory method registers

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,100
a Client named alpha.

4
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,180
The annotation supplies

5
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:08,208
its explicit bean name.

6
00:00:08,288 --> 00:00:09,580
Ask for alpha by name,

7
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,680
and Spring returns that bean.

8
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:12,460
Add the type argument

9
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,390
to check its type too.

10
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:15,660
With just one Client,

11
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:17,240
a type-only lookup returns

12
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,940
the same object.

13
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:19,820
Now register beta

14
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,634
as a second Client.

15
00:00:21,714 --> 00:00:23,220
Both beans have clear names,

16
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,980
but both match Client.

17
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:26,380
With no primary selected,

18
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:28,953
this type-only lookup is ambiguous.

19
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:30,640
Our tests verify named results

20
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,220
and type failure.

21
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:33,440
Names identify beans;

22
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,945
they don't resolve this type tie.

23
00:00:37,945 --> 00:00:39,036
Thanks for watching.

